        {
          "id": 1761597133,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The pre-checkin tests are failing because of a hiccup with the license check.\n\nBefore this change:\n\n```\n$ tools/licensecheck.pl -l 150 tools/make-packet-dcm.py\ntools/make-packet-dcm.py: GENERATED FILE\n```\n\nWith this change:\n\n```\n$ tools/licensecheck.pl -l 150 tools/make-packet-dcm.py \ntools/make-packet-dcm.py: UNKNOWN\n```\n\nLooks like `tools/licensecheck.pl` is spuriously picking up on the \"Generated automatically\" comment here:\n\n```c\npacket_dcm_h = \"\"\"/* packet-dcm.h\n * Definitions for DICOM dissection\n * Copyright 2003, Rich Coe <richcoe2@gmail.com>\n * Copyright 2008-2018, David Aggeler <david_aggeler@hispeed.ch>\n *\n * DICOM communication protocol: https://www.dicomstandard.org/current/\n *\n * Generated automatically by \"\"\" + os.path.basename(sys.argv[0]) + \"\"\" from the following sources:\n *\n```\n\nand deciding that the script itself is generated, however my change causes that text to move from line 149 to line 152, out of the horizon of `tools/licensecheck.pl`, hence it is now `UNKNOWN`.\n\nSuggestions?\n\n(At least I'm assuming it was spuriously being declared a `GENERATED FILE` before... I suspect the generator script itself should have a separate license of its own...?)",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f0f4a609abaf984c9cfe277f1321b8db104aea7290fcbb7fb0c5749a00d32e39?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dariusd0"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-02-07T06:11:06.516Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-02-08T03:00:37.284Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 280366013,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
